# Data Model Rules

The project uses a layered `ProjectData` architecture. The legacy `BrandData` and `SnapshotHistoryItem` types have been deleted — do NOT reference them.

## Use These (from `src/app/types/project.ts`)

- `ProjectData` — top-level state container
- `ElementId` — union type for element identifiers
- `ElementsState` / `ElementSlot<T>` — per-element variation slots
- `Variation<T>` — a single variation with data, source, and metadata
- `SnapshotItem` — a frozen composition snapshot
- `BrandBriefData` — brand brief + target audience + keywords
- `DirectionVersion` / `DirectionState` — output direction layer
- `ElementDataMap` — maps `ElementId` → concrete data type
- `MergeBrandContext` — API payload shape for merge/comment endpoints (from `utils/merge-logic.ts`)

### Helper functions (prefer these over manual slot traversal)

- `getActiveVariation(elements, elementId)` — current active variation
- `getActiveElementData(elements, elementId)` — active variation's data
- `getCheckedVariation(elements, elementId)` — checked variation for snapshot
- `resolveSnapshotData(project, snapshotId)` — hydrate snapshot with element data

## Example

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — types no longer exist
import { BrandData } from "../types/brand";
import { SnapshotHistoryItem } from "../types/app";

// ✅ GOOD — uses new model with typed accessor
import { getActiveElementData, type BrandBriefData } from "../types/project";
import type { MergeBrandContext } from "../utils/merge-logic";
const color = getActiveElementData(project.elements, "color-palette");
```
